&lt;i&gt;Here they come on the southern wind&lt;/i&gt;

19
00:01:17,940 --> 00:01:21,986
&lt;i&gt;Bouncing at the beach&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;Jiggling at the beach&lt;/i&gt;

20
00:01:23,321 --> 00:01:24,447
&lt;i&gt;Want you!&lt;/i&gt;

21
00:01:28,242 --> 00:01:33,998
REIKO'S ON THE HUNT!

22
00:01:37,668 --> 00:01:39,962
Coming through! Move!

23
00:01:42,673 --> 00:01:43,716
Wait for me!

24
00:01:44,467 --> 00:01:46,302
Woohoo!

25
00:01:49,514 --> 00:01:53,059
The rev counter's at one million! It's entering the red zone!

26
00:01:53,267 --> 00:01:57,480
Powering up to two million!

27
00:01:57,897 --> 00:01:59,857
Hang on for a 90-degree turn!

28
00:02:09,116 --> 00:02:12,537
Hey, you kids! Watch where you're going!

29
00:02:21,045 --> 00:02:23,714
You should stop before turning a corner like that.

30
00:02:24,090 --> 00:02:28,928
Look right, then left, to make sure no cars are coming.

31
00:02:29,136 --> 00:02:30,596
-Okay? -Let's get outta here!

32
00:02:33,015 --> 00:02:35,101
Watch out for cars, you hear!

33
00:02:36,811 --> 00:02:38,437
Oh, I'm late!

34
00:02:43,150 --> 00:02:45,861
Ryo-chan will be mad if I'm late for the shift change.

35
00:02:46,070 --> 00:02:47,572
Hello, Reiko-chan!

36
00:02:48,406 --> 00:02:50,408
Good morning! Is your husband better?

37
00:02:50,616 --> 00:02:54,745
His fever has come down, so he'll be back to work again in two or three days.

38
00:02:54,954 --> 00:02:58,708
It can't be easy doing it all on your own. Please look after your health.

39
00:02:58,916 --> 00:03:00,543
-Okay, take care! -Wait!

40
00:03:01,085 --> 00:03:04,839
We're very grateful for how you always look out for us.

41
00:03:05,047 --> 00:03:07,300
It's not much, but please take these.

42
00:03:07,508 --> 00:03:12,305
But I'm supposed to be at work by twelve. Now I'll definitely be late.

43
00:03:12,513 --> 00:03:14,807
-Here you go. -Thank you very much!

44
00:03:15,516 --> 00:03:17,810
Reiko-chan is such a good girl, isn't she?

45
00:03:18,352 --> 00:03:21,772
Girls as kindhearted as her are rare nowadays.

46
00:03:21,981 --> 00:03:25,067
She's got her head on straight, and she's a looker too!

47
00:03:25,276 --> 00:03:28,029
I wish I could trade my own daughter-in-law for her.

48
00:03:28,237 --> 00:03:30,072
Indeed.

49
00:03:32,783 --> 00:03:34,702
Wait a moment, please!

50
00:03:36,037 --> 00:03:38,205
Come now. Let's cross together.

51
00:03:38,414 --> 00:03:43,711
Oh, thank you! I know there's a pedestrian bridge, but it's so far out of the way.

52
00:03:44,211 --> 00:03:47,715
There are so many cars here. You've really saved me.

53
00:03:47,924 --> 00:03:52,053
They're putting some lights in soon, so you won't need to bear much longer.

54
00:03:53,387 --> 00:03:54,722
Hurry it up, will ya!

55
00:03:58,476 --> 00:04:00,061
Wait here for me, please.

56
00:04:00,269 --> 00:04:01,646
Um, okay.

57
00:04:05,983 --> 00:04:06,859
What was that?

58
00:04:07,068 --> 00:04:08,277
No, I was just...

59
00:04:08,486 --> 00:04:11,739
This lady has been waiting for a long time to cross the road.

60
00:04:11,948 --> 00:04:14,367
You'd think you could wait at least 30 seconds?

61
00:04:14,575 --> 00:04:15,910
O-Okay...

62
00:04:16,118 --> 00:04:18,913
Thank you for your cooperation!

63
00:04:22,833 --> 00:04:25,086
Thank you very much.

64
00:04:25,294 --> 00:04:27,380
No problem! Be careful, okay?

65
00:04:28,964 --> 00:04:32,134
Thank goodness! Reiko-san, can you come with us?

66
00:04:32,343 --> 00:04:35,763
"KINDERGARTEN"

67
00:04:41,060 --> 00:04:43,145
"KATSUSHIKA SPEED FREAKS"

68
00:04:44,021 --> 00:04:46,399
It's been parked like this for a while now.

69
00:04:46,607 --> 00:04:50,319
It's in front of the kindergarten, and it's not safe for kids to cross.

70
00:04:50,528 --> 00:04:53,155
We've told them to move, but they won't listen.

71
00:04:53,364 --> 00:04:56,659
And right in the middle of the crosswalk! Have they no shame?

72
00:04:57,284 --> 00:05:02,623
&lt;i&gt;Will the owner of the car parked outside&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;the kindergarten please move it at once.&lt;/i&gt;

73
00:05:16,303 --> 00:05:17,888
"BROKEN DOWN"

74
00:05:18,431 --> 00:05:22,727
So you see, we're waiting on a pal.

75
00:05:22,935 --> 00:05:24,729
He works as a mechanic nearby.

76
00:05:24,937 --> 00:05:26,480
He should be here soon.

77
00:05:26,689 --> 00:05:29,567
That's exactly what you said yesterday.

78
00:05:29,775 --> 00:05:30,985
We know you're lying.

79
00:05:31,485 --> 00:05:33,154
Driver's license, please.

80
00:05:33,362 --> 00:05:37,742
Can't you look the other way? I can't afford any more points on my license.

81
00:05:38,242 --> 00:05:41,203
You Kameari girl cops sure are sweet things, aren't ya?

82
00:05:41,704 --> 00:05:45,207
So you refuse to move your car or provide your license, correct?

83
00:05:47,251 --> 00:05:49,879
I just told you it won't move!

84
00:05:50,629 --> 00:05:53,466
Then I shall move it myself.

85
00:06:02,391 --> 00:06:03,726
What's that thing?

86
00:06:06,312 --> 00:06:09,231
It's actually a cylinder for an air jack.

87
00:06:11,650 --> 00:06:15,446
But if I set it to max, I can inflate it as big as I like. On!

88
00:06:30,669 --> 00:06:32,838
Hey! Stop that, you idiot!

89
00:06:33,047 --> 00:06:36,467
Oh, I don't know how. It's my first time using it.

90
00:06:40,096 --> 00:06:41,138
Uh oh!

91
00:06:50,022 --> 00:06:51,857
Damn it!

92
00:06:55,027 --> 00:06:56,153
You bitch!

93
00:07:09,750 --> 00:07:12,253
Think you can jerk us around, do ya?

94
00:07:15,881 --> 00:07:17,341
You got some sexy legs.

95
00:07:24,014 --> 00:07:26,851
Make that "dangerous legs"!

96
00:07:29,979 --> 00:07:32,982
This ain't the end of this!

97
00:07:33,190 --> 00:07:36,694
Of course it isn't. You still need to pay a fine.

98
00:07:36,902 --> 00:07:38,362
Ah! Oh no!

99
00:07:43,033 --> 00:07:44,368
Welcome back.

100
00:07:45,744 --> 00:07:48,038
You're late. Very late!

101
00:07:48,247 --> 00:07:50,166
I'm sorry, Ryo-chan!

102
00:07:50,374 --> 00:07:54,003
Your shift started at twelve, but it's already gone one o'clock.

103
00:07:54,670 --> 00:07:56,922
I'm very tired from working the night shift.

104
00:07:57,131 --> 00:07:59,967
What's more important, patrolling or my wellbeing?

105
00:08:00,509 --> 00:08:03,470
But you're in there round the clock, even after a shift change.

106
00:08:06,974 --> 00:08:12,354
The chief is up at HQ today, so Ryo-san likes to think he's in charge.

107
00:08:13,147 --> 00:08:15,941
Ah! I'm going on patrol!

108
00:08:16,859 --> 00:08:18,652
Say, I'm getting hungry.

109
00:08:21,822 --> 00:08:24,074
You took your sweet time getting back,

110
00:08:24,283 --> 00:08:27,661
so I didn't even get to go out for lunch.

111
00:08:28,329 --> 00:08:32,124
Hey, don't overcook the noodles. And I want lots of spring onion.

112
00:08:32,333 --> 00:08:37,129
I didn't forget my shift, you know. I just got caught up.

113
00:08:37,338 --> 00:08:39,673
One issue led to another.

114
00:08:39,882 --> 00:08:41,258
Hey, Reiko.

115
00:08:42,718 --> 00:08:44,136
What is it, Ryo-chan?

116
00:08:44,345 --> 00:08:46,347
Pass me that newspaper, would you?

117
00:08:46,680 --> 00:08:49,141
Wouldn't it have been easier to do it yourself?

118
00:08:49,850 --> 00:08:54,396
Some men were illegally parked, and they wouldn't move their car.

119
00:08:54,605 --> 00:08:57,608
They wouldn't take me seriously just because I'm a woman.

120
00:08:58,901 --> 00:09:01,111
While you're here, could you rub my back?

121
00:09:01,487 --> 00:09:02,446
What?

122
00:09:04,365 --> 00:09:08,285
A little lower. Yeah, lower. No, not there. Yes, that's it.

123
00:09:08,494 --> 00:09:11,580
Harder. Yeah, right there.

124
00:09:11,789 --> 00:09:13,207
Like this?

125
00:09:13,874 --> 00:09:19,380
Ugh, no. You're really bad at this. No wonder people don't take you seriously.

126
00:09:20,089 --> 00:09:21,590
How is this even related?

127
00:09:21,799 --> 00:09:25,594
You need a strong and imposing presence when you're out on patrol.

128
00:09:25,803 --> 00:09:28,347
You just don't have that.

129
00:09:30,182 --> 00:09:32,851
I've got an itch. Scratch right around there.

130
00:09:33,060 --> 00:09:33,769
Here?

131
00:09:33,978 --> 00:09:35,646
That's it.

132
00:09:36,146 --> 00:09:39,608
Hey, how's the ramen going? Make sure you don't overcook it.

133
00:09:39,817 --> 00:09:41,986
Oh, I've got another itch...

134
00:09:42,194 --> 00:09:43,612
Ow! What was that for?

135
00:09:43,821 --> 00:09:46,365
I need to be strong, huh? Then take this!

136
00:09:49,743 --> 00:09:51,870
Ugh, so annoying! I swear I'll hit you.

137
00:09:52,079 --> 00:09:53,539
And I'll dodge you!

138
00:09:55,749 --> 00:09:57,042
What's all that for?

139
00:09:57,376 --> 00:10:00,546
They're for throwing at you. I made them myself.

140
00:10:00,754 --> 00:10:01,714
What?

141
00:10:08,429 --> 00:10:09,221
Take that!

142
00:10:13,017 --> 00:10:14,143
Ow!

143
00:10:14,935 --> 00:10:16,478
What do you think?

144
00:10:17,521 --> 00:10:20,315
I think you've let your guard down! Counterattack, go!

145
00:10:21,442 --> 00:10:23,944
Witness the real power of a man!

146
00:10:24,987 --> 00:10:26,697
You coward!

147
00:10:27,114 --> 00:10:28,657
Do you give up?

148
00:10:31,201 --> 00:10:32,786
Oh, we're only just beginning.

149
00:10:33,620 --> 00:10:35,998
If I can't overpower you, I will outlast you.

150
00:10:37,916 --> 00:10:40,210
Take that! And that! And that!

151
00:10:40,419 --> 00:10:43,714
Okay, I get it! That's enough! I give up!

152
00:10:43,922 --> 00:10:45,174
I'm not done yet!

153
00:10:46,175 --> 00:10:48,719
She's really vindictive.

154
00:10:53,265 --> 00:10:54,224
Hello?

155
00:10:54,433 --> 00:10:55,684
&lt;i&gt;I... I saw your poster.&lt;/i&gt;

156
00:10:55,893 --> 00:10:58,520
Huh? Do you have the right number?

157
00:10:59,188 --> 00:11:00,564
&lt;i&gt;You're Reiko, right?&lt;/i&gt;

158
00:11:00,773 --> 00:11:01,648
Who are you?

159
00:11:01,857 --> 00:11:03,317
&lt;i&gt;Will you go out with me?&lt;/i&gt;

160
00:11:03,525 --> 00:11:07,529
What?! Who are you? How did you get this number?

161
00:11:07,738 --> 00:11:09,907
&lt;i&gt;It was on the poster.&lt;/i&gt;

162
00:11:10,115 --> 00:11:11,200
What was that about?

163
00:11:11,408 --> 00:11:12,201
Who was it?

164
00:11:12,409 --> 00:11:15,704
No clue. Something about a poster. What a strange call...

165
00:11:17,122 --> 00:11:17,915
Hello?

166
00:11:18,123 --> 00:11:19,249
&lt;i&gt;Is this Reiko?&lt;/i&gt;

167
00:11:19,458 --> 00:11:20,417
Who even are you?

168
00:11:21,293 --> 00:11:23,170
&lt;i&gt;We could go to the beach together.&lt;/i&gt;

169
00:11:23,378 --> 00:11:24,546
I'll do no such thing.

170
00:11:24,755 --> 00:11:26,090
&lt;i&gt;The mountains, then?&lt;/i&gt;

171
00:11:26,298 --> 00:11:27,841
Go date yourself!

172
00:11:28,675 --> 00:11:31,011
What the heck is this? Ugh, so annoying.

173
00:11:31,220 --> 00:11:33,931
No introduction and just "Go out with me"? So rude!

174
00:11:34,139 --> 00:11:35,349
A date?

175
00:11:36,016 --> 00:11:36,934
Give me the phone.

176
00:11:38,602 --> 00:11:39,353
&lt;i&gt;Reiko?&lt;/i&gt;

177
00:11:39,561 --> 00:11:41,397
That's right. You want a date?

178
00:11:41,605 --> 00:11:42,564
&lt;i&gt;Y-Yes please!&lt;/i&gt;

179
00:11:42,773 --> 00:11:45,609
All right. That'll be 5,000 yen for a first date—

180
00:11:47,111 --> 00:11:49,613
Cut this crap, or I'll arrest you!

181
00:11:49,822 --> 00:11:50,697
Reiko-san!

182
00:11:50,906 --> 00:11:51,782
Huh?

183
00:11:52,241 --> 00:11:54,535
I found these everywhere outside.

184
00:11:54,743 --> 00:11:56,120
What is it?

185
00:11:59,206 --> 00:12:05,003
"HI, I'M REIKO! I'M WAITING FOR YOUR CALL."

186
00:12:10,884 --> 00:12:15,055
So those guys were calling you because they all saw this.

187
00:12:15,514 --> 00:12:17,683
What a crappy candid photo.

188
00:12:17,891 --> 00:12:18,976
I wonder who did it?

189
00:12:19,184 --> 00:12:24,231
I took down a bunch, but there are still loads of them up along the main road.

190
00:12:24,773 --> 00:12:27,526
They're sure going all out. Reiko, any ideas?

191
00:12:27,776 --> 00:12:29,736
How should I know?

192
00:12:29,945 --> 00:12:31,947
&lt;i&gt;This is Naoko! This is Naoko!&lt;/i&gt;

193
00:12:32,156 --> 00:12:33,699
&lt;i&gt;Somebody, please respond!&lt;/i&gt;

194
00:12:34,199 --> 00:12:34,992
Huh?

195
00:12:41,540 --> 00:12:43,625
Suspicious man found driving a dump truck.

196
00:12:43,834 --> 00:12:47,379
We are currently in pursuit, heading north toward Kameari.

197
00:12:47,588 --> 00:12:48,964
Requesting backup.

198
00:12:52,468 --> 00:12:56,471
The driver was putting up posters of Reiko-san.

199
00:12:57,806 --> 00:13:00,976
Copy that! We'll head them off and trap them from both sides.

200
00:13:13,405 --> 00:13:14,364
How horrible!

201
00:13:14,948 --> 00:13:17,034
It's a parade of Reikos.

202
00:13:27,419 --> 00:13:30,964
&lt;i&gt;They're looking both ways&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;before crossing. What good kids.&lt;/i&gt;

203
00:13:35,469 --> 00:13:39,431
&lt;i&gt;Reiko-san, we lost the dump truck.&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;Do you see it anywhere?&lt;/i&gt;

204
00:13:39,640 --> 00:13:40,349
Huh?

205
00:13:44,478 --> 00:13:45,896
Could that be it?

206
00:13:52,444 --> 00:13:53,570
Quickly, Ryo-chan!

207
00:13:54,363 --> 00:13:55,239
W-What is it?

208
00:13:59,076 --> 00:14:00,452
Watch out!

209
00:14:26,728 --> 00:14:27,521
Are you okay?

210
00:14:27,729 --> 00:14:29,064
Yes, I'm fine.

211
00:14:29,273 --> 00:14:30,774
Thank goodness.

212
00:14:31,441 --> 00:14:34,278
Look! My arm's all scratched up.

213
00:14:34,486 --> 00:14:36,822
Ouch! And my back hurts.

214
00:14:38,407 --> 00:14:40,075
You'll pay for this!

215
00:14:43,287 --> 00:14:45,747
Reiko, calm down.

216
00:14:45,956 --> 00:14:47,291
Man, that smarts.

217
00:14:47,708 --> 00:14:50,085
Quickly. Put your seat belt on.

218
00:14:50,627 --> 00:14:52,337
We should call this in first.

219
00:14:53,005 --> 00:14:57,259
This is Ryotsu. Currently in pursuit of a dump truck with an Adachi license plate.

220
00:14:57,467 --> 00:15:00,846
&lt;i&gt;That driver is the one who was&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;putting all those posters up.&lt;/i&gt;

221
00:15:01,054 --> 00:15:04,808
All right, let's box them in. You take National Route 6 and head for—

222
00:15:06,977 --> 00:15:09,313
I told you to put your seat belt on.

223
00:15:12,149 --> 00:15:13,942
Ouch!

224
00:15:21,366 --> 00:15:22,909
You're not getting away!

225
00:15:30,667 --> 00:15:32,419
Got him!

226
00:15:32,628 --> 00:15:34,921
&lt;i&gt;Dump truck! Hold it right there!&lt;/i&gt;

227
00:16:00,113 --> 00:16:02,491
Damn, they weren't wrong about this chick.

228
00:16:02,824 --> 00:16:04,868
Reiko, what happened back there?

229
00:16:05,077 --> 00:16:08,955
Listen up, you two! You almost ran those children over!

230
00:16:10,123 --> 00:16:11,208
And this.

231
00:16:11,416 --> 00:16:13,960
What do you have against me?

232
00:16:14,169 --> 00:16:15,962
It's nothing against you...

233
00:16:16,963 --> 00:16:19,466
Then why were you posting these all over town?

234
00:16:19,675 --> 00:16:20,967
Reiko-san!

235
00:16:21,343 --> 00:16:23,303
Over there. Look.

236
00:16:25,055 --> 00:16:26,306
Ah! It's them!

237
00:16:26,515 --> 00:16:27,724
Who are they?

238
00:16:27,933 --> 00:16:29,559
Damn it. They saw us.

239
00:16:31,061 --> 00:16:32,354
They're the ringleaders.

240
00:16:32,562 --> 00:16:34,064
-You handle these guys. -Okay!

241
00:16:34,272 --> 00:16:35,607
Come on, Ryo-chan!

242
00:16:43,740 --> 00:16:45,700
It's the car I was telling you about.

243
00:16:45,909 --> 00:16:48,370
The hooligans who were illegally parked, huh?

244
00:16:48,578 --> 00:16:51,123
They have terrible taste in cars too.

245
00:16:51,331 --> 00:16:53,917
That kind of car belongs in a dusty old museum.

246
00:17:01,925 --> 00:17:04,386
So much for broken down. Back on track, are we?

247
00:17:04,594 --> 00:17:05,387
Shut up!

248
00:17:08,056 --> 00:17:10,142
After them! Don't let them get away!

249
00:17:10,684 --> 00:17:14,521
I would have destroyed that car if I'd known this was going to happen.

250
00:17:18,734 --> 00:17:21,153
Damn it. This cop chick just won't quit.

251
00:17:24,156 --> 00:17:25,741
Not very gallant, are we?

252
00:17:25,949 --> 00:17:28,243
You're the one who chose violence.

253
00:17:28,577 --> 00:17:30,745
You damaged our car over a parking issue!

254
00:17:31,079 --> 00:17:33,498
All complaints are handled at the police station.

255
00:17:33,707 --> 00:17:34,750
That's right!

256
00:17:34,958 --> 00:17:36,752
To hell with this!

257
00:17:39,588 --> 00:17:40,589
Hold it right there!

258
00:17:44,468 --> 00:17:45,844
Settle down, Reiko!

259
00:17:46,052 --> 00:17:50,724
Look, I agree with you, but this car is a mini. It's only got a 550cc engine.

260
00:17:50,932 --> 00:17:53,685
Theirs must be at least 2,000cc. We'll never catch them!

261
00:17:56,521 --> 00:17:58,648
Hey. She's still following us.

262
00:18:01,651 --> 00:18:05,614
She's no ordinary cop chick. She's on a whole 'nother level!

263
00:18:05,822 --> 00:18:07,199
Get on the expressway.

264
00:18:07,407 --> 00:18:09,659
No way their car will keep up then.

265
00:18:16,333 --> 00:18:19,586
They're going on the expressway. We can't follow them in this.

266
00:18:20,337 --> 00:18:21,505
This is Reiko.

267
00:18:21,713 --> 00:18:24,174
&lt;i&gt;Yes, this is the Kameari Park&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;Police Station.&lt;/i&gt;

268
00:18:24,382 --> 00:18:26,927
Kei-chan, I need a favor.

269
00:18:30,847 --> 00:18:32,891
We can't even see them anymore.

270
00:18:33,099 --> 00:18:34,684
Hey! Reiko!

271
00:18:37,562 --> 00:18:38,688
This isn't good.

272
00:18:38,897 --> 00:18:40,816
Quick! Pull over!

273
00:18:46,863 --> 00:18:48,448
Here he comes. Over here!

274
00:18:50,700 --> 00:18:53,161
An Audi Quattro?

275
00:18:53,370 --> 00:18:55,163
Sorry I'm late.

276
00:18:55,539 --> 00:18:57,832
It just arrived yesterday.

277
00:18:58,041 --> 00:19:01,211
This is the car that won the Montecarlo Rally.

278
00:19:01,419 --> 00:19:04,506
I talked a collector into giving it to me, and—

279
00:19:04,714 --> 00:19:06,132
Right. I'll bring it back.

280
00:19:06,341 --> 00:19:07,467
O-Okay...

281
00:19:14,808 --> 00:19:19,062
The coast was clear for a while, but now some other car is following us.

282
00:19:19,396 --> 00:19:21,314
H-Hey, don't tell me they...

283
00:19:26,486 --> 00:19:27,362
Sorry, sport.

284
00:19:27,571 --> 00:19:29,197
Keep going! Almost there.

285
00:19:29,406 --> 00:19:30,115
Huh?

286
00:19:30,323 --> 00:19:31,867
What is it? What happened?

287
00:19:34,452 --> 00:19:38,081
We're almost out of gas. Ugh, this is so frustrating!

288
00:19:38,290 --> 00:19:42,002
What the hell, Nakagawa! At least fill her up before handing her over.

289
00:19:42,210 --> 00:19:44,754
And there's no gas stations on the expressway.

290
00:19:47,424 --> 00:19:48,884
Hey, found us some gas!

291
00:19:49,092 --> 00:19:50,510
Reiko, slow down.

292
00:19:50,719 --> 00:19:52,971
We'll get some gas from that tanker behind us.

293
00:19:53,179 --> 00:19:54,139
What?

294
00:20:01,980 --> 00:20:03,189
What are they doing?

295
00:20:03,398 --> 00:20:06,568
Damn it. Traffic's jammed. I can't get through!

296
00:20:07,027 --> 00:20:11,448
At 100 yen per liter, it's 4,500 yen for 45 liters, right?

297
00:20:11,656 --> 00:20:13,283
Reiko, give me 4,500 yen!

298
00:20:13,992 --> 00:20:15,577
Keep the change!

299
00:20:16,953 --> 00:20:18,079
Keep it?

300
00:20:18,288 --> 00:20:20,832
That means she doesn't want it, right?

301
00:20:21,499 --> 00:20:23,918
In that case, I'll keep the change!

302
00:20:27,631 --> 00:20:29,257
You little pests.

303
00:20:30,634 --> 00:20:32,802
Quick, the money! Give me my change!

304
00:20:33,011 --> 00:20:34,304
Ryo-chan, get in already!

305
00:20:36,932 --> 00:20:40,310
Give me my change! That's my money!

306
00:20:40,518 --> 00:20:43,146
That change is mine!

307
00:20:44,981 --> 00:20:47,192
Oh, my money!

308
00:20:50,737 --> 00:20:51,946
Here they come again.

309
00:20:52,155 --> 00:20:54,115
I'm sick of this!

310
00:20:54,783 --> 00:20:56,159
Damn it.

311
00:20:57,661 --> 00:21:00,330
Oh no! My money!

312
00:21:00,914 --> 00:21:02,749
Damn those guys!

313
00:21:05,919 --> 00:21:07,879
That's cute. You think you can run?

314
00:21:08,088 --> 00:21:10,256
Reiko, after them! You have my permission!

315
00:21:12,008 --> 00:21:16,262
Hey, wait. Wrong way! You're going against traffic!

316
00:21:16,471 --> 00:21:18,264
This is too much, Reiko!

317
00:21:21,518 --> 00:21:23,436
"INDOOR SKIING"

318
00:21:30,985 --> 00:21:32,654
Whoa! What's going on?

319
00:21:36,282 --> 00:21:39,744
Damn it... This lowrider can't drive on snow.

320
00:21:39,953 --> 00:21:43,248
Let's see how high we can get that car, hey?

321
00:21:48,837 --> 00:21:49,879
Stop it, Reiko!

322
00:21:50,088 --> 00:21:54,050
Pushing another car up a snow ramp is too much, even for an Audi!

323
00:22:08,064 --> 00:22:10,150
Whoa! Please, no!

324
00:22:10,358 --> 00:22:12,152
We're sorry! Please! Someone help!

325
00:22:12,360 --> 00:22:14,446
I'm scared!

326
00:22:15,613 --> 00:22:18,867
Let this be a lesson— never underestimate a woman!

327
00:22:19,409 --> 00:22:22,412
&lt;i&gt;Note to self.&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;Keep Reiko on your good side.&lt;/i&gt;

328
00:22:24,247 --> 00:22:28,251
Well, we got up here, but how are we going to get down?

329
00:22:38,595 --> 00:22:40,346
"KATSUSHIKA POLICE HEADQUARTERS"

330
00:22:40,555 --> 00:22:44,976
Good morning!

331
00:22:45,185 --> 00:22:47,228
We finished waxing it.

332
00:22:48,229 --> 00:22:49,189
Good job.

333
00:22:49,397 --> 00:22:51,274
What's gotten into them?

334
00:22:51,483 --> 00:22:53,818
They were so impressed by Reiko-san's driving

335
00:22:54,027 --> 00:22:56,154
that they wanted to become her students.

336
00:22:57,989 --> 00:23:01,701
I haven't had a scare like that in a long time.

337
00:23:02,744 --> 00:23:05,705
You guys had better watch your back with Reiko too.

338
00:23:05,914 --> 00:23:07,248
-Got it? -Sure.

339
00:23:07,457 --> 00:23:09,042
Ryo-chan, did you call?

340
00:23:09,918 --> 00:23:11,461
Here, I made some tea.

341
00:23:12,045 --> 00:23:15,256
Reiko-san, as always, thank you for making such delicious tea.

342
00:23:15,465 --> 00:23:17,634
Thank you very much!

343
00:23:18,009 --> 00:23:19,761
What lovely weather!

344
00:23:20,428 --> 00:23:21,513
Be careful!

345
00:23:21,721 --> 00:23:23,389
We know!

346
00:23:24,808 --> 00:23:27,060
Oh, it's you. From before.

347
00:23:27,268 --> 00:23:29,729
Thank you for helping me the other day.

348
00:23:29,938 --> 00:23:31,106
You're very welcome.

349
00:23:31,314 --> 00:23:32,607
Reiko-chan.

350
00:23:32,816 --> 00:23:34,776
Oh, hello. What's the matter?

351
00:23:34,984 --> 00:23:37,779
I met a man who'd be a perfect match for you.

352
00:23:37,987 --> 00:23:38,780
What?

353
00:23:38,988 --> 00:23:41,741
You're at a perfect age to be thinking about marriage.

354
00:23:41,950 --> 00:23:43,326
Oh, you...

355
00:23:44,160 --> 00:23:45,119
Say...

356
00:23:46,120 --> 00:23:49,082
I pity the poor sap who ends up marrying her.

357
00:23:49,290 --> 00:23:50,375
Agreed.

358
00:23:53,586 --> 00:23:56,464
TODAY'S DAMAGE REPORT

359
00:23:56,673 --> 00:24:02,220
TWO CARS

360
00:24:04,180 --> 00:24:05,807
&lt;i&gt;The Olympics are this year!&lt;/i&gt;

361
00:24:06,015 --> 00:24:09,102
&lt;i&gt;And the Olympics means Higurashi.&lt;/i&gt;

362
00:24:09,310 --> 00:24:12,355
&lt;i&gt;He's a fellow colleague&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;at Kameari Park Police Station.&lt;/i&gt;

363
00:24:12,564 --> 00:24:14,941
&lt;i&gt;But he only ever wakes&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;once every four years.&lt;/i&gt;

364
00:24:15,149 --> 00:24:18,695
&lt;i&gt;But you'll never believe&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;what his special ability is!&lt;/i&gt;

365
00:24:18,903 --> 00:24:20,905
NEXT EPISODE WAKE UP, HIBERNATING COP!

366
00:24:21,114 --> 00:24:22,949
&lt;i&gt;Don't miss it!&lt;/i&gt;

367
00:24:32,917 --> 00:24:37,172
&lt;i&gt;Let's keep smiling always&lt;/i&gt;

368
00:24:37,839 --> 00:24:41,426
&lt;i&gt;Even when things go wrong&lt;/i&gt;

369
00:24:41,676 --> 00:24:45,930
&lt;i&gt;Keep a pretty smile on your face&lt;/i&gt;

370
00:24:46,556 --> 00:24:50,977
&lt;i&gt;And go out as if nothing happened&lt;/i&gt;

371
00:24:51,519 --> 00:24:55,106
&lt;i&gt;Hey, show me your smile&lt;/i&gt;

372
00:24:55,315 --> 00:24:59,235
&lt;i&gt;You did nothing wrong&lt;/i&gt;

373
00:25:00,236 --> 00:25:03,781
&lt;i&gt;Hey, show me your smile&lt;/i&gt;

374
00:25:03,990 --> 00:25:07,660
&lt;i&gt;Just like you did before, yeah&lt;/i&gt;

375
00:25:07,869 --> 00:25:12,040
&lt;i&gt;I want you to smile always&lt;/i&gt;

376
00:25:12,749 --> 00:25:17,212
&lt;i&gt;A woman with a frown isn't pretty&lt;/i&gt;

377
00:25:17,712 --> 00:25:23,259
&lt;i&gt;So you should smile as soon as you can&lt;/i&gt;

378
00:25:24,052 --> 00:25:27,013
&lt;i&gt;It's the grown-up thing to do&lt;/i&gt;

379
00:25:39,150 --> 00:25:43,863
KOCHIKAME SEE YOU NEXT TIME!
